// zig/hello_world's wire type -- deliberately the simplest possible payload
// (an incrementing count plus a fixed string), unkeyed, single instance.
// See docs/design/hello-world-reference-app.md at the repo root for the
// full spec. Byte-identical copy required in c/hello_world, cpp/hello_world,
// java/hello_world once those ports exist (same discipline shape.idl
// already follows across bindings).
//
// No @key: per DDS 1.4 2.2.2.1, "If no key is provided, the data set
// associated with the Topic is restricted to a single instance" -- a
// keyless Topic is fully spec-legitimate, not a corner case, and zidl's
// --generate-zzdds-wrappers now generates DataWriter/DataReader for it
// (fixed in zidl/src/backend/zig.zig -- see isZzddsTopicStruct and
// emitStructSerializeFns' --generate-zzdds-wrappers branch; previously it
// required a @key, which had this example keying on `message` as a
// workaround -- no longer needed).
@appendable
struct HelloWorld {
    int32 count;
    string<256> message;
};
